<title>SWEDEN: S&amp;P says Sweden ratings unaffected by EMU decision.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P says Sweden ratings unaffected by EMU decision.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit ratings agency Standard &amp; Poor's said on Tuesday Sweden's sovereign ratings would not be affected by its decision not to join Europe's economic and monetary union (EMU) from its planned 1999 start.  </p>
<p>The managing director of Standard &amp; Poor's in Stockholm, Marianne Flink, told Reuters the EMU decision would have no impact on Swedish ratings.</p>
<p>The Swedish government appeared to be ready to continue with tight fiscal policy, S&amp;P said.</p>
<p>&quot;We see an intention to follow strict fiscal policy and this is positive,&quot; Flink said.</p>
<p>In April Standard &amp; Poor's raised its outlook for Sweden's foreign currency rating to stable from negative.</p>
<p>-- Erik Aronsson, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1010</p>
